SUMMARY:Mills River-BRP: Spencer Gap & Ferrin Knob  6 miles\, 1225’ asce
 nt
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Directions:** From I-26\, exit 3
 3 (Blue Ridge Parkway\, Brevard Rd) : South on Brevard Rd (NC-191) for 2.4
  miles to the light at the Arboretum / BRP entrance. Turn Right (West) on 
 the BRP to trailhead\n**Trailhead: Bent Creek Gap**: BRP milepost 400.3 at
  Bent Creek Gap Rd--take the gravel road on the left to park under the ove
 rpass. Departing on time: 8:30. Look for Silver Lincoln SUV. Cell: 239-777
 -4743\n**Details**: Hike south of the BRP from Bent Creek Gap Road into th
 e Mills River area\, and then north of the BRP over Ferrin Knob. Some rock
 y footing and fairly steep climbs up Trace Ridge and Ferrin Knob. Starting
  from BRP milepost 400.3: Walk down the National Forest Rd for 1-3/4 miles
  to a right on Spencer Gap trail\; then up Trace Ridge trail for a short d
 istance to the BRP. Pickup the Mountain-to-Sea Trail on the north side of 
 the BRP opposite Beaverdam Gap Overlook. Climb Ferrin Knob for a snack bre
 ak\, and return to the trailhead. Type: Loop **Max elev:** 4000’. Avg mo
 ving pace: 2.4 mph. Difficulty (1=effortless\, 10=hard): 5. Dogs: welcome 
 if well-behaved\, leashed\, and subject to area restrictions. **Option of 
 having a beer/lunch at the Stoneridge tavern following the hike**\n**\\*\\
 *Courtesy** (Please read carefully!)\\*\\* Only sign up if you \\\\\\*trul
 y\\\\\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\, please change your status to "
 Not Going" as soon as possible. Avoid dropping out within 24 hours so that
  wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't b
 e a no-show.\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hik
 ing and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participa
 nts are responsible for their own safety and affirm that they have the app
 ropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking
  may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer no
 r Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. B
 y signing up for this event\, participant understands and agrees.
