SUMMARY:MST Walker Knob Overlook/Balsam Gap - Route 128\, 8.5mi\, 2\,300ft
  FITNESS HIKE
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nOne may recall how dry this trail 
 was last time. Recent rains have returned its natural moist glory.\n\nCar 
 poolers will meet at the Bull Creek Valley Overlook (just past the Tanbark
  Ridge Tunnel) on the Parkway at 9:00am. The hike will start at the Walker
  Knob Overlook on the Parkway. Please let the hike leader know where you i
 ntend to meet us: carpool spot (9:00am) or trailhead (9:30am).\n\nAny rain
  cancellation or venue change will be made by 7:30am.\n\nOut and back hike
 . The trail elevates quickly and then undulates along a ridge of the Black
  Mountain chain. Expect to see lots of moss\, ferns\, and fungi. Some of t
 he trail is rocky\; some is soft moss and pine needle carpet.\n\nWe will s
 top for lunch at the Allen Rinas overlook\, a rather prominent rock outcro
 pping with a great view over the Asheville watershed (see photo) near the 
 4mi point\, and turn around there.\n\nMore ambitious hikers are welcome to
  continue the approximately one mile (and 350ft.) descent to Route 128\, a
 nd turn around there.\n\nWe will be near 6\,000ft elevation and under fore
 st cover for most of the hike.\n\nPACE: Fitness hikes proceed at a steady 
 BRISK pace adjusting for steepness of grade. PLEASE BE IN SHAPE AND CAPABL
 E OF HIKING THIS DISTANCE WITH ELEVATION. This is not a hike for beginners
 . If your interests include outdoor fitness hiking for cardio conditioning
  and endurance join us.\n\nDOGS: Dogs are welcome as long as they are trai
 l friendly.\n\nIF YOU SIGN ON THIS HIKE AND CHANGE YOUR MIND (EVEN IF YOU 
 ARE ON THE WAITLIST) GO BACK TO THE RSVP LINK AND CHANGE YOUR STATUS TO FR
 EE UP YOUR RESERVED SPOT.\n\nRelease of Liability:\nThe organizer of this 
 trip is volunteer and is not a professional guide. The function of the org
 anizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in thi
 s event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume al
 l risks of injuries\, illnesses and damages arising from\, as a result of 
 and associated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledging that you a
 gree to the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.com/terms\n\nThis is a Level 
 7 hike.\n*Hike Levels:Level 1\; 300-600 feet elevation gain\; Level 2 600-
 900'\; Level 3\, 900-1200"\; Level 4\; 1200-1500' Level 5\; 1500-1800' LEV
 EL 6\; 1800-2100' Level 7*\; 2100-2400' Level 8\; 2400-2700' Level 9\; 270
 0-3000' Level 10\; 3000-4000' ULTIMATE HIKES\; > 4000'
