SUMMARY:Strawberry Gap 5.2 mi.\, 1\,200  ft. elev. gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Sign-up opens Sunday\, Aug. 2nd 
 @ 8:00 PM**\n\nThis is a somewhat strenuous out-and-back hike\, with nearl
 y all of the uphill being on the "out" part. We'll do a moderate pace of a
 round 2.3 mph\, with breaks as needed and a 15-minute snack/water break at
  or near the turn-around point. It's a typical walk in the woods for these
  parts (which is to say\, beautiful!)\, and the payoff at the top -- Blue 
 Ridge Pastures -- has a panoramic view of the surrounding mountains.\n\n**
 *Dog Policy:*** Sorry\, but dogs are officially prohibited on this trail.\
 n\n***Guest Policy:*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, they should join t
 he Asheville Hiking Group and sign up for the hike on their own. Alternati
 vely\, contact me in advance and ask if it's okay to bring a "+1" after yo
 u've made it onto the "Going" list. Depending on timing and demand\, I may
  be able to add your guest.\n\n**CARPOOLING TIME & PLACE**\nThere's ample 
 parking at the lot by the trailhead\, but let's carpool anyway so that our
  large group doesn't fill it up.\n\nHere's a link to the [carpool location
  on Google Maps](https://www.google.com/maps/place/Food+Lion/@35.5253197\,
 -82.4138144\,17z/data=!3m1!4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x8859f0403dcd4c65:0xd1ae595dd417
 bfc5!8m2!3d35.5253197!4d-82.4112341!16s%2Fg%2F1tdw45t5?hl=en&entry=ttu).\n
 \n* We'll meet **8:45 AM** at the Food Lion parking lot\, 1350 Charlotte H
 ighway (Rt. ALT-74) in Fairview.\n* Gather at the side of the lot **closes
 t to the Highway**\, furthest from the store.\n* We **depart Food Lion jus
 t after 8:45 AM**\, so please arrive before that time. It's about 10 minut
 es from there to the trailhead.\n\n**Directions from Asheville**\n\n* Take
  Alt 74 East toward Fairview.\n* From the intersection with I-40 and I-240
 \, you'll be on ALT-74 for 6.7 miles. Food Lion is on the left.\n\n**Direc
 tions from Hendersonville**\n\n* US 25 North to Fletcher\, right turn onto
  Cane Creek Rd.\n* In 8.7 miles\, turn left onto Alt-74\, Charlotte Highwa
 y\n* Food Lion is less than a mile on the right\n\n**COURTESY TO WAIT-LIST
 ERS (Please abide!)**\nOnly sign up if you \\*TRULY\\* plan to come. If yo
 u must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Going" as possible so wa
 it-listers can have sufficient notice. And please please PLEASE don't be a
  no-show.\n\nIf you're on the waiting list\, keep checking the evening bef
 ore. Despite what I wrote above\, we always get last-minute dropouts.\n\n*
 *WEATHER**\nI'll monitor the National Weather Service forecast for the hik
 e area. If the forecast calls for a> 50% chance of rain or temps below 25\
 , I'll email cancellation messages by 7:30 AM.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nIf you h
 ave any questions\, message me through MeetUp. Cell reception may be sketc
 hy\, but you can try to text or call me up to the start of the hike: (803)
  767-3094.\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \n\n**LEGALESE**\n\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\
 , possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are 
 responsible for their own safety and\, by joining a hike\, affirm that the
 y have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and su
 pplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hik
 e organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can eliminate all risks or be respo
 nsible for your well-being. Participants assume full responsibility for an
 y injuries\, damages\, or losses.
